      "attributes": {
        "id": 380,
        "relationship_type": "related",
        "body": "ましょうか and Verb [よう] are both volitional forms, with ましょうか being polite and Verb [よう] (sometimes with か) casual. ～ましょうか is used to make polite suggestions like 'Shall we...?' (e.g. 行きましょうか = 'Shall we go?') 行こうか is more casual and introspective, often expressing the speaker's internal thoughts (e.g. 'Should I go?')",
