        "relationship_type": "related",
        "body": "Both of these use Verb [よう], the volitional form, to express suggestions like 'Let's do (A).' The core meaning is the same, but they differ in tone. Verb [よう] is casual and used in everyday speech among friends. In contrast, ～ようではないか has a tone that sounds more formal and grandiose, and will be found in media or situations where the speaker is looking for dramatic effect.",
